      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes we do, since pvm_psci_vcpu_on() sets the power_state to PSCI_0_2_AFFINITY_LEVEL_ON_PENDING, and then pkvm_reset_vcpu() sets the mp_state KVM_MP_STATE_RUNNABLE.\n\nMaybe we want to review the whole protocol and setting of these flags, but at least for now, this seems the like simplest (i.e., least risky) change.",
