        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T12:59:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If `flush_hyp_vcpu()` sees a vCPU in the `ON_PENDING` state, it will reset it and transition it to `ON` so I think we should move that logic out and check the `power_state` in `handle__kvm_vcpu_run()` directly. What do you think?\n\nFor newer kernels, we could probably remove all the `mp_state` tracking at EL2 as I don\u0027t think it\u0027s used for anything other than some redundant assertions.",
      "parentUuid": "70e0daad_33b7ed34",
      "range": {
